            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Abdus Salam</strong><br>\nAbdus Salam was born in Jhang, a city in what is now Pakistan, in 1926. He was a child prodigy, excelling in mathematics and science. His talents were recognized early, and he received a scholarship to attend Government College University in Lahore. There, his passion for physics began to take shape. He graduated with top honors, setting him on a path to become a prominent physicist.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Education and Early Career</strong><br>\nAfter completing his education in Lahore, Salam went to the United Kingdom for further studies. He attended St John's College, Cambridge, where he earned a degree in mathematics with first-class honors. Salam then obtained his PhD in theoretical physics from Cambridge University. His thesis contributed to the field of quantum electrodynamics, which was a major area of research at the time.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Quantum Electrodynamics Work</strong><br>\nSalam's work in quantum electrodynamics, or QED, was significant. QED is a theory that describes how light and matter interact. His early research helped to lay the groundwork for future discoveries. He focused on developing a renormalizable theory of quantum field theory, which would later be important for the advancement of particle physics.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
