          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Advocacy for Science in the Islamic World</strong><br>\nSalam was passionate about improving the status of science in Islamic countries. He believed that a historical golden age of science in the Islamic world could be reignited. Salam spent considerable effort in advocating for the education and development of science in these regions, emphasizing the importance of scientific knowledge.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Personal Challenges and Beliefs</strong><br>\nDespite his global recognition, Salam faced personal challenges because of his Ahmadi faith. In Pakistan, Ahmadis are considered non-Muslims, which led to Salam's marginalization in his home country. However, he remained committed to his scientific endeavors and his faith, often speaking about the compatibility of science and religion.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy and Influence</strong><br>\nAbdus Salam's legacy extends beyond his scientific achievements. He left an indelible mark on the world through his advocacy for science and his efforts to inspire young scientists, especially in the developing world. His vision for a global scientific community continues to influence young minds and institutions dedicated to scientific research and collaboration.</p>\n"
              },
